Original commit body from 0d2cbccc170828953e6a1d03d98456256b61c1cb:

The callback branch of js_ts's enclosing lookup built its position key
without the <script> block's line_offset. Every other branch adds it. So
in a .vue or .svelte file the key named a line `offset` lines ABOVE the
callback. When another callback started there at the same column, the
call was credited to it: koel's HotkeyListener.vue, the last 9
typescript call edges outside their src's span (INV-midag). Otherwise
the walk went on and credited the enclosing function or the file.

Correction to the row: it said the callback symbols were positioned
without the offset. They are positioned correctly. The LOOKUP is what
lacked it, and it matched a neighbouring callback.

The decision the row asked for: make .vue match .js. A callback is
credited with its own calls in .js by design (WI-zavad, the anonymous
callback symbols exist for exactly that). The other option, crediting
the enclosing function in both, would undo that design for .js.

A/B, analyze_javascript from a pinned dev worktree vs this tree, calls
edges keyed by (path, dst, line):
  koel            OUT->in 9, file->callback 279
  chatwoot        enclosing fn->callback 7
  podman-desktop  file->callback 78, enclosing fn->callback 11
  workadventure   file->callback 55, enclosing fn->callback 15
  gitlab          file->callback 2, enclosing fn->callback 115
No edge added or lost on any repo, and no in->out move. Every move is a
relabel into the innermost function containing the call.

Also re-pins the two line citations below the edit
(signature_axis js_ts 5358 -> 5362, module_key_axis 6547 -> 6551).

